        </ol>
      </div>
      <div class="prose-content text-lg leading-relaxed text-primary" data-aos="fade-up"><h2 id="sec-1">Quick Overview</h2><p>Standing desk converters let you transform any existing desk into an ergonomic sit-stand workstation. We tested 12 converters for stability, ease of adjustment, build quality, and value.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Rank</th><th>Product</th><th>Price</th><th>Rating</th><th>Height Range</th><th>Weight Capacity</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1</td><td><strong>VariDesk Pro Plus 36</strong></td><td>$495</td><td>⭐ 4.8/5</td><td>6-20 inches</td><td>35 lbs</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td><strong>FlexiSpot M2B</strong></td><td>$249</td><td>⭐ 4.7/5</td><td>4.7-19.7 inches</td><td>33 lbs</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td><strong>Fully Jarvis</strong></td><td>$349</td><td>⭐ 4.6/5</td><td>5-18 inches</td><td>30 lbs</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td><strong>FEZIBO Dual Motor</strong></td><td>$299</td><td>⭐ 4.5/5</td><td>5-19 inches</td><td>35 lbs</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td><strong>Uplift V2 Standing</strong></td><td>$399</td><td>⭐ 4.6/5</td><td>6-17 inches</td><td>29 lbs</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td><strong>Seville Classics AirLift</strong></td><td>$199</td><td>⭐ 4.3/5</td><td>5-15 inches</td><td>26 lbs</td></tr><tr><td>7</td><td><strong>ErgoChair Pro</strong></td><td>$179</td><td>⭐ 4.2/5</td><td>4-14 inches</td><td>22 lbs</td></tr><tr><td>8</td><td><strong>Mount-It! MI-EM3001</strong></td><td>$149</td><td>⭐ 4.1/5</td><td>5-15 inches</td><td>25 lbs</td></tr><tr><td>9</td><td><strong>VIVO Vertical</strong></td><td>$129</td><td>⭐ 4.0/5</td><td>4-12 inches</td><td>20 lbs</td></tr><tr><td>10</td><td><strong>Amazon Basics Gas Spring</strong></td><td>$89</td><td>⭐ 3.9/5</td><td>3-10 inches</td><td>18 lbs</td></tr></tbody></table><h2 id="sec-2">How We Evaluated</h2><p>Each converter was tested for two weeks: stability during typing and writing at standing height, adjustment smoothness (gas spring vs manual), platform size for dual monitors and accessories, build quality and materials, assembly time, and overall value.</p><h2 id="sec-3">Top Picks Reviewed</h2><h3>1. VariDesk Pro Plus 36 — Best Overall</h3><p>The VariDesk Pro Plus 36 is the industry standard. Gas spring mechanism provides buttery-smooth height adjustments, and the dual-tier design with pull-out keyboard tray accommodates most setups. The 36-inch platform fits dual monitors comfortably with 15-year warranty backing.</p><div style="background:#F7F4EF;border-left:3px solid #C9A962;padding:1rem 1.25rem;margin:1.5rem 0;border-radius:0 8px 8px 0"><p style="margin:0;font-size:0.95rem"><strong>Best for:</strong> Professionals who spend 8+ hours daily at their desk and want the most stable, durable solution.</p></div><h3>2. FlexiSpot M2B — Best Value</h3><p>At $249, the FlexiSpot M2B delivers premium features at nearly half the VariDesk price. Gas spring adjusts smoothly from 4.7 to 19.7 inches. The 31-inch platform handles dual monitors with room to spare. Integrated cable management keeps workspaces tidy.</p><h3>3. FEZIBO Dual Motor — Best Heavy Setups</h3><p>With 35-pound weight capacity, the FEZIBO handles multiple monitors and heavy equipment without sagging. Dual gas spring mechanism ensures smooth, balanced lifting throughout the entire height range.</p><h2 id="sec-4">Benefits of Standing Desks</h2><ul><li><strong>Reduced back pain:</strong> Standing improves posture and reduces lumbar strain</li><li><strong>Increased energy:</strong> Standing boosts circulation and alertness</li><li><strong>Better metabolism:</strong> Standing burns 50-60 more calories per hour than sitting</li><li><strong>Improved mood:</strong> Studies show reduced fatigue and improved well-being</li></ul><h2 id="sec-5">FAQs</h2><h3>How much time should I stand?</h3><p>Aim for 20-30 minutes per hour. The ideal pattern is 40 minutes sitting followed by 20 minutes standing.</p><h3>Will a converter fit my desk?</h3><p>Most work on desks 1-2.5 inches thick. The FlexiSpot M2B accommodates 0.5 to 2.5 inches.</p><h2 id="sec-6">Final Verdict</h2><div style="background:linear-gradient(135deg,#1A1A1A 0%,#2A2A2A 100%);color:white;padding:2rem;border-radius:12px;margin-top:2rem"><p style="font-family:'Playfair Display',serif;font-size:1.5rem;font-weight:700;margin:0 0 0.75rem 0;color:#C9A962">Our Recommendation</p><p style="margin:0;line-height:1.8">The <strong>FlexiSpot M2B</strong> at $249 is the best value for most people. For the absolute best, the <strong>VariDesk Pro Plus 36</strong> at $495 is worth the premium for serious professionals.</p></div></div>
